Well, I don't have a Mac to create ChrHack with, I have an IBM.  :-)

I suppose doing ChrHack for Mac would be as easy as creating a new font
and telling McNethack to use the new font.  The code for ChrHack is
very machine dependant and won't work on non-IBM based graphics systems.

As far as color goes, ChrHack doesn't modify the color that is used, just
the symbol.  Scream at the Dev Team if you want color changed. 
